Date: 2025-12-08
Session: Go TUI Timesheet Application Development

Prompt:
I want you to make me a go tui application that provides the basic timesheet history and capture functions provided by our kartoza timesheet web app, but replicating it as a go / bubbletea application. https://github.com/kartoza/timesheet-project

Also you can use these components to make a rich, user friendly experience in the terminal:

https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/ntcharts
https://github.com/charmbracelet/huh
https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/ntcharts
https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbles
https://github.com/76creates/stickers
https://github.com/daltonsw/bubbleup
https://github.com/calyptia/go-bubble-table
https://github.com/KevM/bubbleo

For now the scope of work is to reverse engineer the kartoza timesheet-project react application and implement the functionality shown in the three screenshots I attach:

timesheet-entry.png
timesheet-listing.png
timesheet-submission.png

You do not need to follow the visual style of the original.

The app should be able to be launched with various utility calls to so that I can have a waybar icon to start the app ready to start work on a task, show a running indicator when my timesheet is being recorded, show an idle indicator when my timesheet is not active. Later I am going to ask you to implement some smart logic such that when I enter and stay in a virtual desktop in my wayfire desktop for more than 5 seconds, it automatically starts logging time against a particular project and task which will be parsed from the workspace name.

The layout of the bubbletea app should be responsive through the use of the 76creates/stickers responsive grid layout.

Please log this prompt and every other instruction I give you in prompt.log

Action Taken:
- Logged prompt to PROMPT.log for comprehensive session tracking
